\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Probability of correctly ordering two systems as a function of their true quality gap (log axis), for five representative judges ordered by resolution limit. Black: both systems rendered in the same style. Teal: styles assigned independently at random. Orange: the worse system wears the judge's preferred style. Dashed grey marks the measured resolution limit. \textbf  {Takeaway:} the adversarial curve is a step, and its location---not the judge's average accuracy---is what determines whether a leaderboard gap means anything.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:curves}{{2}{7}{Probability of correctly ordering two systems as a function of their true quality gap (log axis), for five representative judges ordered by resolution limit. Black: both systems rendered in the same style. Teal: styles assigned independently at random. Orange: the worse system wears the judge's preferred style. Dashed grey marks the measured resolution limit. \textbf {Takeaway:} the adversarial curve is a step, and its location---not the judge's average accuracy---is what determines whether a leaderboard gap means anything}{figure.2}{}}
